      "Abstract": {
        "CopyrightInformation": "Copyright © 2013 Journal of Pediatric Urology Company. Published by Elsevier Ltd. All rights reserved.",
        "AbstractText": "Chronic scrotal pain can be a difficult clinical entity to treat. Many different treatment options have been proposed. We describe the case of a young boy with chronic scrotal and inguinal pain on the right side, following two orchidopexies. After many therapies had failed, we treated the dorsal root ganglia of thoracic 12, lumbar 1 and lumbar 2 with pulsed radiofrequency, finally resulting in alleviation of his pain."
      },
